# tally 2.2 (CHANGES.md 2.2-10, pick P14): the fault's fix is at the trimming, and the dependency graph is tally
# 2.1.8's. A def keyed by an event kind whose at binds over the kind, an ask with no law: LOAD-LAWDATE, as tally 2.1.8
# refuses it (an edge for the def's key had let it answer). Expect: tally 2.1.8's refcore, byte for byte.
=== m.tally
model n3
  tally 2
  on 2025-04-01
  start 2025-03-01
  end 2025-03-31
  note "N-3 probe: a def keyed by an event kind whose at binds over the kind, with an observed input; an ask with no law reads it."

source s "s"
unit DUK: currency minor 0.01
place konto: accounts DUK lives 2025-03-01..
place world: outside lives 2025-03-01..
input bank: observed
input mo: month
input d1: date
input amt: money DUK
input f: money DUK

def fee[t in transfers]: money DUK = f at max(x.day for x in transfers over mo)

move m1: transfers
  on d1
  leg cash from world to konto amount amt

ask q: sum(fee[t] for t in transfers over mo)

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2025-03-01
  mo = 2025-03 "s"
  d1 = 2025-03-05 "s"
  amt = 10.00 "s"
  f = 1.00 "s"
  opening[konto] = 0.00 at 2025-03-01 start "s"
=== expect
refused: LOAD-LAWDATE ask q reaches fee, whose at reads law-dated facts at its reader's law date, without law (L §4.3) (m.tally:24)
